{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1787080685,"nonce":"GAVuSM2k11wbS9N7L6tsr2COGBk=","title":"`baseline.txt` still exempts `Thread.SubjectKind`, whose reader arrived with the digest thread, and a baseline line matching nothing is itself a failure","message":"**What is wrong.** `tools/lintreach/baseline.txt:145` reads:\n\n    noread:github.com/thulasiram/oto/internal/notification/domain.Thread.SubjectKind\tfield is never read in production — the value goes nowhere (internal/notification/domain/thread.go:133)\n\nThe debt was paid. `internal/notification/service/dispatch.go:739` reads it in production: `case mode == domain.ModePostRoot \u0026\u0026 th.SubjectKind == domain.SubjectDigest \u0026\u0026 th.RootLanded():` — the arm that keeps a digest root from being amended, added with the digest thread of migration 00058. The finding no longer exists, and `lintreach` treats a baseline line that matches nothing as an error in its own right: `tools/lintreach/main.go:122-125` — *\"a baseline line that matches nothing is itself an error, so a paid debt cannot keep its exemption\"* — implemented at `:221-225` and `:258-260`, which prints *\"matches nothing — the debt was paid; delete the line\"* and exits 1.\n\n**The demonstration.** Run, not read. `go run ./tools/lintreach -report -v` on this branch reports `248 known debt` against a `baseline.txt` holding **249 distinct keys**; the one key that never matches is `noread:…domain.Thread.SubjectKind`. Diffing the `known debt` lines against the file's first column leaves exactly that entry and nothing else — the five odd-looking `go-only:` and `spec-only:` keys all appear in the run's output and are accounted for.\n\nThe stale-line message does not print on the current tree only because `main.go:243-245` exits at the type-error gate first: the working tree has eleven type errors in `_test.go` files still referencing `SuppressorStorm`, `SuppressorFlapping`, `ReasonStorm` and `Reason.Retired`, which is separate in-flight work and not this ticket. Once the tree compiles, `just lint-reachability` fails on this line, and `ci` (`justfile:374`) fails with it.\n\n**Why it matters.** It is a one-line fix, but the rule it violates is the one that makes the baseline trustworthy. The baseline is an assertion that every line on it is a finding that still exists and whose fix belongs elsewhere; a line that has quietly stopped being true turns the file from a debt register into a list of claims nobody checks. And it fails closed rather than open — the gate goes red for a reason that has nothing to do with whatever change is being made — which is how a team learns to ignore a gate.\n\nThe same run reports three `new` findings — `CasePolicy.OrgID`, `PlanInput.Flapping` and `DigestConfig.Limit` — which are the retire-in-place collision tracked separately, not this. This ticket is the one line whose debt is simply paid.\n\n**Where.** `tools/lintreach/baseline.txt:145` (the line) · `internal/notification/service/dispatch.go:739` (the reader that paid it) · `internal/notification/domain/thread.go:133` (`Thread.SubjectKind`, the field the line names) · `tools/lintreach/main.go:122-125` (the rule), `:221-230` (`stale`), `:258-260` (the message and the exit) · `justfile:345-346`, `:374`.\n\n**Scope.** small — delete one line.\n\n**Done when.** `tools/lintreach/baseline.txt` no longer carries `noread:…domain.Thread.SubjectKind`, and `go run ./tools/lintreach` reports no stale entry, on a tree that type-checks.","files":null}]}